 "reading_text": "The user wants me to read the time from an analog clock image. Let me carefully examine the clock face.\n\nLooking at the image, there are three hands: an hour hand (short, white), a minute hand (long, white), and a second hand (thin, red).\n\nLet me look at the positions:\n- The long white hand (minute hand) points almost straight up, just slightly past the 12, toward the 12-1 region but very close to 12. Actually it looks like it's pointing just past 12, maybe at the 2-3 minute mark? Let me look. The minute hand is near the top, pointing slightly right of 12. That would be around 1-2 minutes.\n- The short white hand (hour hand) points straight down at 6. So the hour is around 6.\n- The red second hand points to about the 1 (upper right), around the 6-7 second mark.\n\nSo the hour hand at 6 and minute hand near 12 (just past) suggests the time is approximately 6:01.\n\n",
